Description:

Adds HTTP/3 (RFC 9114) support to httpd via the "-3" command line option.
Also includes support for WebSockets over HTTP/3 (RFC 9220).


Documentation:

docsrc/concepts/features/quic-dispatch.rst.


Config changes:

New imapoptions: quic_ebpf, quic_ebpf_iface, quic_idle_timeout,
http_h3_altsvc.

New cyrus.conf service type: proto="quic" for an "httpd -3" service.

New configure options:

  --without-nghttp3       disable HTTP/3 (QUIC) support
  --without-quic-ebpf     disable eBPF-based per-connection QUIC
                          dispatch in master (falls back to a
                          userspace relay)


Upgrade instructions:

Opt-in: add a proto="quic" service to cyrus.conf to enable. Requires
ngtcp2/nghttp3 (built against OpenSSL 3.5+ for native QUIC TLS) at
build time; eBPF dispatch additionally needs libbpf/libcap and clang.


